+# VOICE-DAY-ONE — the ordered path from an Azure credential to a real likeness number
+
+**WS-R188 (wave twenty-four).** Voice quality is the most important single
+thing in this product (`context/STATE.md`), and the voice program has been
+blocked on an Azure credential for a week. `evals/rehearsal/voice-dry-run.mjs`
+proves the whole path — enrol, process, a candidate produced, one paired
+listening verdict, the activation guard, "Hear the vibe", a Room reply spoken
+sentence by sentence — connects, offline, against the deterministic fake
+providers this repo already ships. This file is the companion runbook for the
+day someone actually has the credential: what to set, what
+`scripts/voice-day-one.mjs` does, what the receipts look like, and where a
+REAL likeness number will land. It never prints a value, and it costs nothing
+to read.
+
+**Read alongside, never instead of:** `docs/gurukul/ENV-MANIFEST.md` §7-12
+(the exact file:line every name below is read at), `docs/gurukul/DAY-ONE.md`
+(the general infrastructure-then-product runbook this file specializes for
+voice), `context/STATE.md` (the current LIVE state), and
+`evals/rehearsal/voice-dry-run.mjs`'s own header (what is proven offline,
+what is a named, deliberate gap).
+
+## What to set
+
+`scripts/voice-day-one.mjs` (no args, or `--live`) is the single source of
+truth for the required set — it exports `REQUIRED_VOICE_ENV` as a table of
+`{name, section}` and refuses by name, never running anything, until every
+one of them is present. Do not retype this list anywhere else; if it drifts
+from `docs/gurukul/ENV-MANIFEST.md` §7-12, the manifest is the fix, and the
+script's own comment cites the exact section for each name.
+
+At a glance, the required set spans five real subsystems, each independently
+gating a step of the SAME path the dry run walks offline:
+
+| step in the dry run | live subsystem (ENV-MANIFEST.md section) | var names |
+|---|---|---|
+| enrol + process (voice evidence extraction) | §10 voice evidence | `AZURE_VOICE_EVIDENCE_ORIGIN`, `AZURE_VOICE_EVIDENCE_HMAC_SECRET` |
+| a candidate is produced (Azure Personal Voice creation) | §7 | `AZURE_PERSONAL_VOICE_ENABLED`, `AZURE_PERSONAL_VOICE_LIMITED_ACCESS_APPROVED`, `AZURE_PERSONAL_VOICE_ENDPOINT`, `AZURE_PERSONAL_VOICE_TTS_ENDPOINT`, `AZURE_PERSONAL_VOICE_KEY`, `AZURE_PERSONAL_VOICE_PROJECT_ID`, `AZURE_PERSONAL_VOICE_COMPANY_NAME`, `AZURE_PERSONAL_VOICE_BASE_MODEL` |
+| candidate + "Hear the vibe" spend fencing | §8 | `AZURE_REPLICA_APP_BUDGET_USD`, `AZURE_PERSONAL_VOICE_USD_PER_PROFILE`, `AZURE_PERSONAL_VOICE_SYNTHESIS_USD_PER_MCHARACTERS` |
+| synthesis (the PRIMARY lane, `VOICE_LANE_ORDER`'s own self-hosted-first order) | §9 | `AZURE_OPEN_VOICE_ORIGIN`, `OPEN_VOICE_HMAC_SECRET` |
+| every derived audio byte written anywhere in the path | §12 | `SUPABASE_URL`, `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, `REPLICA_STORAGE_BUCKET` |
+| everything reads/writes through | database | `NEON_URL` |
+
+This workstream's own brief describes the gating set loosely as "Azure
+Foundry and Speech keys, the subscription and tenant ids." Checked against
+`docs/gurukul/ENV-MANIFEST.md` directly rather than assumed: **Foundry**
+(`AZURE_FOUNDRY_ENDPOINT`/`AZURE_FOUNDRY_API_KEY`) is real and documented
+(§1) but is the claim-extraction/dialogue lane — this dry run's own path
+never reaches it, so it is NOT in `REQUIRED_VOICE_ENV`; it is named in
+`scripts/voice-day-one.mjs`'s own `INFORMATIONAL_VOICE_ENV` for a day-one
+that also drafts a HumanOS sheet from sources in the same sitting. **The
+manifest documents no separate "subscription id"/"tenant id" pair for the
+voice lanes at all** — the one `AZURE_TENANT_ID` name that exists anywhere in
+it is a DIFFERENT subsystem's own setting (`api/_channel-secrets.js`'s
+`keyVaultAuth()`, channel-secret Key Vault auth), so it is also named
+informationally rather than claimed as a voice requirement it is not. Saying
+so here, rather than silently widening `REQUIRED_VOICE_ENV` to match the
+brief's looser wording, is the same law `AGENTS.md` states for every other
+claim in this repo: never claim what was not checked against the file that
+actually reads it.
+
+## What the command does
+
+```
+node scripts/voice-day-one.mjs            # dry-run (default)
+node scripts/voice-day-one.mjs --live     # still refuses without every name
+```
+
+Both forms:
+
+1. Check every name in `REQUIRED_VOICE_ENV` by PRESENCE only (never a value
+   read into a log line) and refuse, listing the missing names and their
+   section, if any are absent.
+2. When every name is present, run the SAME real config validators the
+   product itself calls (`azurePersonalVoiceConfig`,
+   `azurePersonalVoiceErasureConfig`, `openChatterboxConfig`) as a structural
+   check — this catches a malformed value (a non-HTTPS endpoint, a key that
+   is present but too short, a model string still saying "latest") before
+   anything is attempted. It proves nothing about whether the credential is
+   genuinely valid; only Azure can tell you that.
+3. Print the exact spend ceiling this run would honour, read from the SAME
+   three names the real spend fence (`api/_provider-budget.js`) reads —
+   never a second, hand-typed number that could drift from it.
+4. `--live` is out of this workstream's own scope by its own law 5: "the
+   live command is proven to refuse without the env names ... never by
+   running it." Running the path for real, once every name and structural
+   check above is green, is done by hand, door by door — the same real
+   doors `evals/rehearsal/voice-dry-run.mjs` already exercises offline, now
+   pointed at the real Azure lanes instead of the fake ones.
+
+`evals/voice-day-one/run.mjs` proves every refusal above, including spawning
+the real CLI itself with an EMPTY environment (never a credential) and
+checking the exit code and the absence of a stack trace.
+
+## What the receipts look like
+
+Nothing here is invented — every shape below is the real, existing column or
+door the dry run already exercises against the fake provider, restated for
+what a LIVE row means once Azure is the provider instead:
+
+- **A queued, then settled, voice genome build**
+  (`vy_replica_model_build`, `build_kind='voice_genome'`) — the SAME
+  `queueOwnedVoiceGenome` → `leaseNextVoiceGenomeBuild` →
+  `completeVoiceGenomeBuild` chain the dry run drives against a fixture db,
+  now against the real database. Its `source_set_hash` is a real hash over
+  REAL, human-reviewed evidence — the `lower(adapter_family||' '||
+  adapter_name||' '||adapter_version) !~ '(fake|fixture|test|mock)'` gate
+  the dry run's own header names (see "the real finding" there) means this
+  can only ever happen from a real processing adapter's own output, never a
+  rehearsal's.
+- **Two sealed voice_preview generations** (`vy_replica_generation`,
+  `purpose='voice_preview'`, `state='sealed'`) — real audio, real
+  `audio_sha256`, genuinely distinct bytes (unlike the dry run's own fake
+  provider, whose PCM is byte-identical regardless of input text — see the
+  dry run's own header).
+- **One recorded listening verdict**
+  (`recordVoiceListeningVerdict`, `api/_replica-calibration.js`) — the SAME
+  four axes `LISTENING_AXES` names (owner_likeness, naturalness,
+  indian_accent, pronunciation), scored by a real person listening to real
+  audio, not the dry run's own scripted ratings.
+- **An activation decision, possibly overridden**
+  (`guardOwnedVoiceActivation`) — admits the verdict's real winner, or
+  refuses a losing candidate unless a real person explicitly overrides it
+  (logged to `vy_replica_audit` as `voice.activation.override`, never
+  silent).
+
+## Where "likeness measured on a real voice" will land, and what it will mean
+
+`vy_voice_fidelity` (`api/_fidelity.js`, `clientFidelity`,
+`DEFAULT_FIDELITY_POLICY`) is the table and the client-facing shape a real
+likeness score already has everywhere else in this codebase — the listening
+card on the owner's own studio panel reads it through
+`ownedVoiceLikenessSummary` (`api/_replica-voice-preview.js`), the exact
+function `evals/listening-test/run.mjs` already imports and proves offline.
+**A live day-one voice run writes into this SAME table, through this SAME
+reader — no new column, no new door.** What changes is only the SOURCE of the
+number: today, every `vy_voice_fidelity` row in this codebase's own fixtures
+and suites is either absent or explicitly synthetic; a live run is the first
+row this system will have ever written from a real person's real voice,
+scored by a real person's own paired listening choice, never a number a
+model estimated on its own. `context/decisions.md#platform-north-star`'s own
+law stands unchanged by this file: "a measured likeness score is a product
